{
  "//": [
    "contrib/antigravity/hooks.json.example — agy's own hooks schema, NOT",
    "settings.json (compare contrib/claude-code/settings.hooks.json.example,",
    "which merges into Claude Code's settings.json under a top-level 'hooks'",
    "key). Per <https://antigravity.google/docs/hooks>: 'Hooks are configured",
    "in a hooks.json file in your customization directory (e.g. .agents/ in",
    "your workspace or ~/.gemini/config/).' Copy this file's contents (minus",
    "these '//' comment keys, which are not valid JSON and exist here only as",
    "documentation — see the note at the bottom) to one of:",
    "  ~/.gemini/config/hooks.json          (global, all workspaces)",
    "  <workspace>/.agents/hooks.json       (this workspace only)",
    "and fill in the real path to emit.sh (see below). The '//'-prefixed",
    "keys below are valid JSON but are NOT part of agy's hooks.json schema",
    "(they're a comment convention, not a documented field) — strip them",
    "before installing if agy's loader turns out to validate strictly",
    "against unknown top-level keys; 'name', 'enabled', and 'hooks' are the",
    "only keys documented at <https://antigravity.google/docs/hooks>.",
    "",
    "Schema shape: a named wrapper object carrying an 'enabled' flag, then",
    "event names mapping to arrays of { matcher, hooks: [{ type, command,",
    "timeout }] } entries — structurally close to Claude Code's hooks shape,",
    "but the wrapper and the flag are agy-specific.",
    "",
    "Only PreInvocation and Stop are wired here. PreToolUse and PostToolUse",
    "are deliberately NOT wired — see the 'why not PreToolUse/PostToolUse'",
    "note at the bottom before adding them.",
    "",
    "Stop -> emit.sh done: a Stop whose stdin payload carries a non-empty",
    "`.error` field is upgraded from `done` to `attention` INSIDE emit.sh",
    "(it reads `.error` off the same stdin payload it already parses for",
    "`conversationId`/`transcriptPath`), not by wiring a second Stop hook",
    "entry here — a hook's stdin can only be consumed once, so two Stop",
    "commands racing to read it would mean only one ever sees the payload.",
    "See emit.sh's header comment for the full reasoning."
  ],
  "name": "saola-panel-antigravity",
  "enabled": true,
  "hooks": {
    "PreInvocation": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$HOME/Developer/saola-panel/contrib/antigravity/emit.sh working",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$HOME/Developer/saola-panel/contrib/antigravity/emit.sh done",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "//why-not-pretooluse-posttooluse": [
    "PreToolUse's response schema REQUIRES a `decision` field",
    "(allow/deny/ask/force_ask/deny_unless_prior_grant) — it is the one agy",
    "event where a hook's stdout participates directly in the tool-",
    "permission path. A status emitter has no basis to decide whether a",
    "tool call should be allowed, and printing the wrong `decision` (or none,",
    "if a future agy version stops defaulting a missing key to `allow`)",
    "could block or silently alter Jordan's own tool calls. PostToolUse's",
    "contract is just `{}` and would be technically safe to wire, but there",
    "is no status this phase's vocabulary needs it for (Stop already covers",
    "'turn ended') and adding it would only be one more hook invocation per",
    "tool call for no new information. Both are left out on purpose, not by",
    "oversight — do not add PreToolUse without re-reading",
    "<https://antigravity.google/docs/hooks>'s decision contract first."
  ]
}
